# Syncro API keys — copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in what you have.
#
# Two ways to configure, use either (or both — .env values pre-fill the UI):
#   1. Set them here; they are injected into the build at compile time (see vite.config.ts).
#   2. Enter them at runtime in the app's key-entry UI (⚙ key panel) — they are stored
#      only in your browser's localStorage and sent directly to each provider.
#
# Nothing is required to launch the app. Features degrade gracefully and tell you
# which key is missing. See README.md for the full table.

# ── Gemini (Google AI Studio) — https://aistudio.google.com/apikey ──────────
# Powers: clip analysis, key moments, descriptions, Style Bible generation
# (structured output), voiceover generation, and the image-edit fallback for
# object surgery.
# Without it: analysis, captions, and Style Bible generation are unavailable.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Groq (free tier) — https://console.groq.com/keys ────────────────────────
# Powers: Style Bible generation fallback (OpenAI-compatible endpoint).
# Without it: Style Bible generation requires a Gemini key instead.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ── fal.ai — https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys ──────────────────────────────────
# Powers: SAM 2 segmentation + VOID video inpainting for time-ranged object
# removal (the high-quality path).
# Without it: object removal falls back to the Gemini image-edit path.
FAL_KEY=

# ── Replicate — https://replicate.com/account/api-tokens ───────────────────
# Optional: alternate provider account for the inpainting models.
# Without it: fal.ai serves the inpainting path.
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# ── Meshy — https://www.meshy.ai/dashboard/api-keys ─────────────────────────
# Powers: image-to-3D asset generation (frame → GLB) — the preferred provider.
# Without it: 3D insert falls back to Tripo.
MESHY_API_KEY=

# ── Tripo — https://platform.tripo3d.ai/apikey ──────────────────────────────
# Powers: image-to-3D fallback.
# Without it: 3D insert requires a Meshy key.
TRIPO_API_KEY=
